      "reason": "It requires putting the model and WOA23 fields on one grid and applying one common valid-cell mask before cell-by-cell N:P comparisons and regression, and warns about inappropriate land-sea masks.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Put all four fields on one grid, build one mask with `build_comparison_mask`, and apply `.where(mask)` before model–observation/multi-model metrics; report mask cell counts. WOA23 is the reference, so `ocean_only=True` is appropriate.",
        "Coverage is level-specific: build/apply the mask for the 200–1000 m layer, not from the surface; report means from `compute_difference_metrics` on the shared sample, not means over each source's own ocean."
      ]
    },
    {
