      "reason": "It directly constrains the requested basin means, because basin statistics depend on the chosen partition and must state how marginal seas, Southern Ocean and Arctic are treated.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "The CMOR Ofx `basin` field is not local; use the WOA23 mask (`load_basin_mask`, `select_basin`). `include_marginal_seas=True` folds marginal seas into their parent ocean; state this and how Southern/Arctic are treated/excluded.",
        "A named ocean normally uses surface labels applied through the water column (`depth_dependent=False`); each level's own labels (`depth_dependent=True`) are for water-mass analysis. State which choice is used."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "omip-weighted-means-and-integrals",
      "severity": "should",
