      "sha256": "89de52676ae54db8f5897bc77a08c78de3f776696db0020935a38b790c302cbe",
      "reason": "It specifies volume- or mass-weighted means and use of all grid points, which applies to the percentage-of-water-volume metrics and any volume weighting over the 200–1000 m layer.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "For 200–1000 m means use Σ field·`volcello` / Σ `volcello` over valid ocean cells with NaN-aware weights; plain `mean()` is wrong. Headline N:P is the volume-weighted mean of the cell-by-cell ratio; ratio-of-means is the ratio of volume-weighted mean `no3` to mean `po4`; state which is reported.",
        "Volume shares beyond/between N:P thresholds must be shares of volume, not cells, with missing cells out of the denominator; `compute_exceedance_fraction` returns the percentage and the m3 behind it. The requested OLS is equal-cell weighted, as the question states."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "monthly-means-are-time-averages",
      "severity": "must",
      "path": "pitfalls/monthly-means-are-time-averages.md",
      "sha256": "df6b5c23460f88f1522e5c6a665e1efbb8322c3ae876c885530f3019aa284ee0",
      "reason": "It warns that N:P computed from monthly-mean nitrate and phosphate is a nonlinear diagnostic, so the time-averaging order must be stated and can change the result.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Monthly fields are time averages; N:P is nonlinear, so f(monthly mean) ≠ mean of f. State the order: average `no3`/`po4` first then form N:P gives the diagnostic of the mean state and is like-for-like with a WOA climatology; ratio-first reproduces the mean monthly N:P.",
        "For the annual 1971–2000 mean use `temporal_aggregate(freq='mean')`, which applies day weights; equal-weight `mean(dim='time')` is not a time average. A single calendar-month climatology is the plain mean across years."
      ]
    },
    {
